1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,854
Protein variant review starts with a task and explicit limits.

2
00:00:04,024 --> 00:00:10,731
BioPilot Atlas puts constraints, recorded tool decisions, and candidate evidence in one workspace.

3
00:00:10,901 --> 00:00:19,592
This edited browser demonstration shows actual local interactions, saved scientific results marked replay, and
offline synthetic narration.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,219
The public Lipase A reference uses full reference, one based positions.

5
00:00:25,389 --> 00:00:29,327
Its entire sequence is the registered scoring context.

6
00:00:29,497 --> 00:00:32,321
Catalytic sites remain protected.

7
00:00:32,491 --> 00:00:38,200
A separate offline input check validates a declared substitution with the product guards.

8
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:41,759
It does not change the saved scientific run.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,569
Open the decision trace to inspect what the actual Meta model requested.

10
00:00:49,739 --> 00:00:55,697
Muse Spark requested target validation, then the permitted scoring tool through MCP.

11
00:00:55,867 --> 00:01:00,956
Each saved step exposes a short reason, bounded arguments, and result.

12
00:01:01,126 --> 00:01:06,704
Local ESM computed sequence preferences; code applied the common ranking.

13
00:01:06,874 --> 00:01:12,083
Switching steps only changes the replay view and sends no provider request.

14
00:01:12,253 --> 00:01:15,057
No private chain of thought is shown.

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,374
Now change the local check to a protected serine substitution.

16
00:01:24,544 --> 00:01:26,558
The code refuses it.

17
00:01:26,728 --> 00:01:32,661
Declaring mature sequence numbering also requires correction, with no guessed offset.

18
00:01:32,831 --> 00:01:38,445
These are actual local guard interactions, separate from recorded Meta decisions.

19
00:01:38,615 --> 00:01:41,679
The scientific scores stay unchanged.

20
00:01:41,849 --> 00:01:47,452
Protecting catalytic sites is a conservative constraint and does not prove retained function.

21
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,763
Select candidates for side by side review, then inspect the export controls.

22
00:01:55,933 --> 00:02:01,252
Scores, positions, and original ranks come directly from the saved artifact.

23
00:02:01,422 --> 00:02:05,455
Selection creates no new ranking or evidence of improvement.

24
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:14,479
ESM preferences are not T fifty, activity, solubility, melting temperature, or experimental validation.

25
00:02:14,649 --> 00:02:17,863
Unknown atom geometry stays unavailable.

26
00:02:18,033 --> 00:02:22,441
This is an unvalidated sequence evidence assistant for human review.

27
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,379
A separate frozen intake test recorded six closed set cases, with rules supplied.

28
00:02:30,549 --> 00:02:35,022
Local guards answered six of six; Meta, five of six.

29
00:02:35,192 --> 00:02:37,431
The manual arm was not run.

30
00:02:37,601 --> 00:02:44,569
This small rule application test establishes no time saving, scientific skill, or biological gain.

31
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:49,020
Inspect the recorded model, scoring policy, and source hashes.

32
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:51,436
Actual billing remains unknown.

33
00:02:51,606 --> 00:02:56,184
Earlier work stays credited, and publication and submission remain separate.

34
00:02:56,354 --> 00:02:59,574
BioPilot makes its evidence and limits inspectable.

